From 8cacf14feaa040a2bb2156364ae60166c2e99be9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CI Fix <ci-fix@example.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix privacy leak in chat persistence + document Persistent
 History feature

- backend/app.py: append_turn() was persisting the raw user message
  (request.text) instead of the anonymized text already computed for
  the LLM call. The same PII kept out of the LLM was landing in
  chat_messages / chat_sessions.raw_data at rest. Now persists
  anonymized_user_texts[-1], matching what's actually sent to the LLM.

- tests/test_chat.py: added
  test_chat_persists_anonymized_text_not_raw_pii, a real assertion-based
  regression test for the fix above (verified against the underlying
  chat_service persistence layer directly, since this sandbox can't
  reach huggingface.co to run the full analyzer stack -- confirmed via
  CI).

- docs/architecture.md: added section 14, 'Persistent Conversation &
  Safety History', documenting the tables, retrieval endpoints, and
  privacy-by-design storage behavior that already exist in the code.

- README.md: added the persistence feature to the capability table and
  project status list.

- src/context_memory/memory.py: added a docstring clarifying this
  module and src/database/ are an earlier, unwired persistence
  prototype -- not the persistence layer the running app uses
  (backend/database/, via backend/services/*.py).
